 @Davinmk  Why'd you buy a 4090 then instead of a 7900XTX for cheaper? Sure it's a halo card and has the best raster, but you're really going to clown on people for using that still has objective value in some games because it doesn't fit your ideals?

Let's look at this from another angle, why the hell do you use 144hz and not 120hz? Many ppl would say that 144hz is a minute difference, a marginal benefit, but you value it, probably opting for it purely in a competitive setting. You chose what you value, don't trash others for what they value.

Are RT titles limited? Of course, but that doesn't change the fact that many people that buy NVIDIA are purely sold on those specific title. And there are a good number of titles (Cyberpunk, Spider Man Miles Morales, Doom Eternal, RTX Portal and Minecraft, Control) that use RT very well. And, for many people, that's enough to warrant a jump for a stronger RT performer.
